From 53824c199cca54c2147535b02bdf22aba5eb5be7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:48:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: About shows the X2600 variant

AD5X boards come with different X2600 variants: the X2600E has 256 MiB
of DDR3 in the package, the X2600H 512 MiB. Settings -> About now names
it next to the eMMC:

  Processor  X2600E, 256 MiB DDR3, SoC ID 0x18000, core 0.0

The SoC information comes from the eFuse: Kiln's 7.3 kernel exposes it as
the nvmem cell socinfo@6b (20 bits, then the same 20 bits as a check).
Ingenic's 6.6 kernel has no eFuse driver; there the row reads "X2600,
256 MiB, variant unknown", the size from the boot loader's ad5x.ram= when
it gave one. The core revision comes from /proc/cpuinfo. The variant
names are Ingenic's seven; a capacity code of 8 or more shows as an
unknown size. The chip ID in the eFuse is left out: it is a serial
number, and About screenshots get posted.

Kiln builds only (HELIX_KILN_AD5X); elsewhere the row stays hidden.

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
